19: * On this Windows runtime `O_NOFOLLOW` is platform-optional; the measured hardlink protection is
20:   `O_EXCL`. No concurrency/race or broad sandbox guarantee is granted.
21: * The pre-fix artifact-name case leaves the outside sentinel bytes intact because replacement severs
22:   the hardlink; the officer explicitly declines to call that an outside-inode overwrite.
23: * `read-only` in the workflow means no remote mutation, not a literally read-only runner checkout.
24: * The workflow's `pull_request` `paths:` filter is a separate trigger concern, not proof that every PR
25:   reaches the guard.
